<!DOCTYPE html><html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
<head>
  <title>EstRas: Statistical calculations of raster images.</title>
<meta content="text/html; charset=ISO-8859-1" http-equiv="Content-Type"/></head>

<body>
  <!--Aquí inicia la part corresponent al titol de la MSA. Aquesta part s'ha d'editar desde el document WPS (aplicacio.mps).-->
<h1><span id="wpstitol"/></h1>
<!--Aquí acaba la part corresponent titol de la MSA editable de el WPS.-->

 
	<p>This module calculates statistical data of Raster images in which you can choose between three options: 
	The calculation of statistical data of a single raster (monobath or multiband), the calculation of an image with 
	the result of the statistical function chosen in Starting with a series of raster and standardizing a raster (monobath or multi-band).</p>

	<p>For the calculation of statistical data of a single raster, the input file must be an IMG raster file and at least one of the available statistical functions must be selected 
	(depending on the treatment of the data that it is selected). The output file must be an INI file where the result of the different statistical calculations chosen will be written. 
	This option allows you to do this calculation for all bands of a multiband raster file.</p>
	
	<p>For the calculation of an image of the statistics of a series of raster, the input file must be a TXT file with the list of raster files in the IMG format that you want to 
	use for the calculation. There must be at least two raster files to perform the calculation and have the same number of rows and columns. The calculation is done pixel by pixel where for 
	each pixel all the valid values of the pixel that are in the same position in the input rasters are selected and with these values the chosen statistical function is applied and the result 
	is written to the raster output file that must be an IMG raster file.</p>
	
	<p>The option of normalizing a raster, the input file and the output file must be an IMG raster file. This option allows you to do this calculation for all bands of a multiband raster file.</p>
	
	<p>If you want to calculate the frequencies or areas of the different categories of a categorical raster, you can use the Histo module or the query for attributes of the main module of the MiraMon.</p>


  <br/>
  
